@packages/compiler/src/evaluation-capabilities.sigil import { SigilAgentCapabilityContract }

component SigilEvaluationSkillRegistry {
  goal {
    Discover and validate versioned compiler-native evaluation skill packages and
    their rule, evidence, dependency, capability, and output contracts.

    Express required provider capabilities using AgentCapabilityContract.
  }

  interface {
    EvaluationSkillPackage {
      load(stageIdentity, version) returns exactly one EvaluationSkillLoadResult:
      ready with validated EvaluationGuidance, unavailable with reason
      missing-package or missing-version, invalid with reason malformed-guidance,
      malformed-policy, identity-mismatch, incompatible-version, invalid-inputs,
      invalid-dependencies, invalid-capabilities, capability-mismatch, invalid-rules,
      unsupported-policy, or invalid-output-contract, or host-failure with one stable
      non-empty failure code and message

      ready alone permits adapter invocation. unavailable or invalid invokes no
      adapter and produces one incomplete evaluator outcome with the exact load
      reason, marks the selected stage failed, and remains visible in its report
      trace. A failed required stage prevents green; a failed optional stage does not
      prevent green but remains failed and cannot supply dependency evidence

      host-failure rejects the owning compilation operation with COMPILER_FAILED,
      produces no CompilationReport, and follows its operation owner's failed-event
      settlement rather than becoming an evaluator outcome

      implementation-evidence policy is context-only or compare

      required capabilities use the AgentCapabilityContract vocabulary
    }
  }
}

expand SigilEvaluationSkillRegistry {
  constraints {
    EvaluationSkillPackage {
      stageIdentity and version are non-empty exact identities. Invalid caller input
      returns invalid with reason invalid-inputs before package access.

      malformed-policy is reserved for a present compile.json whose syntax, shape, or
      required policy fields cannot be decoded before field-specific validation.

      EvaluationGuidance contains the validated skill identity, exact version,
      instructions, allowed rules, implementation-evidence policy, and output
      contract identity consumed by AgentEvaluationRequest.

      Loading is single-attempt for one stage and version. unavailable and invalid
      results are deterministic package outcomes; inaccessible storage, I/O failure,
      or an undeclared loader failure is host-failure.
    }
  }

  cases {
    EvaluationSkillPackage {
      A missing requested version returns unavailable missing-version and leaves a
      required stage failed and incomplete without invoking an adapter.

      A package with valid guidance but an unknown implementation-evidence policy
      returns invalid unsupported-policy.

      A malformed dependency declaration returns invalid invalid-dependencies; an
      undeclared diagnostic rule returns invalid invalid-rules; a mismatched output
      schema returns invalid invalid-output-contract. Every unequal or undeclared
      capability dimension under AgentCapabilityContract exact matching returns
      invalid capability-mismatch, regardless of whether either value appears more
      permissive.

      An optional stage with unavailable guidance is failed and visible but does not
      by itself prevent green; any dependent stage skips for unavailable evidence.

      A storage read failure returns host-failure and the owning operation returns no
      report.
    }
  }
}
